This commit also carries two changes its message doesn't mention.

A pull request that couldn't be set to auto-merge is now counted as done.
Enabling auto-merge returned an error, so the package was reported as having
generated nothing and the run's budget never went down; every remaining package
then got a pull request of its own, eight before the run was cancelled. The
failure that exposed it was 'Protected branch rules not configured for this
branch', which is what GitHub says about a branch with no required checks.

The branch template moved from templates/pkg to template, and its contents are
now copied to the package branch at the same paths. A workflow lives at
template/.github/workflows/ and lands at .github/workflows/, so the layout of a
package branch is visible in the template rather than only inside ar2.
